          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Catra had never had an easy life. She had grown up in the foster system after losing her fathers, gotten herself pregnant at eighteen after a drunk night at a bar, and couldnâ€™t hold a stable job that paid enough for her shitty three room apartment. She knew she wasnâ€™t built for motherhood. She had never been shown what a good parent looks like, so what made her fit to raise a child on her own? She didnâ€™t think she would be until she met Finn for the first time. Alone in a hospital bed with the tiny one month preemie kitten in her arms was enough. Finn became her everything. She would make it work somehow. Sheâ€™d always made her own way, and she would find a way to give the infant the life they deserved even if it killed her.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It took three jobs, but she made enough to live in a small apartment. Then she lost two of those jobs because money went missing from the drawers and the old diner couldnâ€™t keep its doors open. Small tips at the bar and minimum wage were enough for her, but not her and a five year old. Her landlord was impatient and didnâ€™t care if Catra chose feeding Finn over paying rent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A fight breaks out, a gun is fired.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But who would believe it was the five year old who pulled the trigger?&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
